      "message": "test(plasma): drive the cover-law pin through plasma_profile\n\nRe-review item on #1081: the pin called cover_law directly with the\ntightened tolerance, so reverting cut()'s cover reach to plain KERF_TOL\nstayed green. The pin now cuts a plate whose top edge carries a notch\nnarrower than the kerf; the offset bridges it, and the notch depth is\nset from the bridged cut's own chords (geometry, not the law) so the\nfarthest floor point sits midway between the plain and the tightened\nreach. plasma_profile cuts it at full fidelity and refuses it by name\nat model_excess 0.007; reverting the call site to KERF_TOL fails it.\n\nRefs #1053\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
